  "id": "xavante_auwe_dano_re",
  "name": "A'uwẽ (Xavante) da-ño're and ceremonial song",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Collective ceremonial song of the Gê-speaking A'uwẽ (Xavante) of eastern Mato Grosso, sung above all by groups of men within the age-set system whose initiation cycle (danhono) moves boys into adulthood. The da-ño're are collective songs that the Xavante describe as coming to young men in dreams; the dreamer teaches the song to his age-set, who sing and dance it together, a practice the anthropologist Laura R. Graham analysed in her book Performing Dreams. The Pimentel Barbosa (Etenhiritipá) community released its own recordings as the CD Etenhiritipá: Cantos da Tradição Xavante.",
  "recipe": "classic modern a'uwẽ (xavante) da-ño're and ceremonial song, ritual Devotional, indigenous branch. group vocals. foot stomp. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
